21:["$","section","4-Separate scholarship language rules from course language",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-5","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Separate scholarship language rules from course language"}],[["$","p","Some categories use Japanese or English examinations during screening, and university programmes can set their own language evidence. The absence of IELTS from one central checklist does not prove a universal waiver.",{"children":"Some categories use Japanese or English examinations during screening, and university programmes can set their own language evidence. The absence of IELTS from one central checklist does not prove a universal waiver."}],["$","p","Record the teaching language, accepted evidence and stage at which it is required. Ask the embassy or university only after reading the newest route-specific guidance.",{"children":"Record the teaching language, accepted evidence and stage at which it is required. Ask the embassy or university only after reading the newest route-specific guidance."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
